The Hon'ble Supreme Court of India, in case titled Jaspal Singh Jolly Vs Municipal Corporation of Delhi, reported as 125 (2005) DLT 592, has held that:-
"Noting the decision of the Supreme Court as Erusia Digitally signed Pitamber by Pitamber Dutt Dutt Date: 2026.02.12 18:15:07 +0530 Arun Goyal & Ors Vs State (Through FSO FSAT) Page no. 10 of 12 Equipments & Chemical Ltd. Vs State of West Bengal, (1975) 1 SCC 70: AIR 1975 SC 266 (at P. 269); 106 (2003) DLT 573, Mekaster Trading Corporation Vs Union of India;
and (1990) 4 SCC 594, S.N. Mukherjee Vs Union of India, I had held that the aforesaid decision established the legal proposition that orders which are subject to judicial review must be in compliance with the principle of natural justice, namely (a) proper hearing, (b) decision by an unbiased mind;
(c) taking into consideration all the relevant factors and excluding the irrelevant factors; and (d)
reasons to be recorded.
